    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. but when you say 'polarized', aren't most mainstream economists generally in agreement that the deregulation actually helped unlock productivity and get rid of the stagflation issues from the 70s? feels like the 'inequality' argument is more of a political critique than a consensus on whether the growth itself was real or not.",
