      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While some mainstream views emphasized the anti-inflation and pro-productivity benefits that deregulation provided, the consensus is not perfectly unified on the *primary driver* of the 80s economic upswing. Many argue that the strong policy stance, particularly the Federal Reserve's aggressive interest rate policy, was a more direct and powerful force in taming 1970s \"stagflation\" than the specific acts of market liberalization alone. The debate often then shifts to the *sustainability and distribution* of the growth that followed these policy shifts, rather than the absolute reality of the initial economic gains.",
      "source": "target",
